4. Third-party components
================================================================================

markproof depends on the following third-party packages at run time. They are
installed by pip/uv from PyPI and are NOT vendored or redistributed in this
repository or in the markproof wheel. The complete, generated dependency
license inventory lives in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md and is refreshed per release.

  c2pa-python  (Content Authenticity Initiative)   MIT OR Apache-2.0
      Official bindings for c2pa-rs; loads the prebuilt c2pa-rs native library
      at install time (likewise MIT/Apache-2.0).
  rfc8785      (Trail of Bits)                     Apache-2.0
      RFC 8785 (JCS) canonicalisation used for the report signature.
  cryptography (PyCA)                              Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
  httpx                                            BSD-3-Clause
  pydantic                                         MIT
  typer                                            MIT
  ruamel.yaml                                      MIT

Optional extras, installed only on request:

  transformers (Hugging Face)                      Apache-2.0   [synthid]
  torch                                            BSD-3-Clause a.o.       [synthid]
      SynthID text watermark detection. Models are downloaded at run time; no
      model weights are contained in this repository or in the wheel.
  reportlab                                        BSD-3-Clause [pdf]
  weasyprint                                       BSD-3-Clause [pdf-html]
  playwright                                       Apache-2.0   [ui]
      Browser binaries are downloaded at run time and are not redistributed.

Development-only tools (not distributed with the package): pytest, mypy, ruff,
respx, hypothesis (MPL-2.0), pre-commit, uv, and c2patool (Apache-2.0 OR MIT,
part of contentauth/c2pa-rs) for generating test fixtures.
